{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/743149-purging-a-vampire-of-wyrm-taint","id":743149,"title":"Purging a vampire of Wyrm Taint","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-30T16:04:38-07:00","id":743149,"title":"Purging a vampire of Wyrm Taint","content":"What have you done with the idea of purging vampires of their Wyrm taint? What <i>would </i>you do with it? Say you take a vampire to the endless silver night of Erebus and plunge them into the molten silver lake. She emerges whole, unbroken by trial, perhaps reforged instead. What happens? Does the vampire gain more control over her Beast? Does she become a creature wholly different from what she was before? Good or ill, what do you think happens with the vampire?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T16:28:25-07:00","id":743202,"title":"","content":"Since Erebus is for werewolves only I would imagine a vampire would ash when you dumped it in the lake since its molten silver and the resident spirits of justice would probably toss you in next for contaminating their fondue pot of redemption.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T16:48:40-07:00","id":743232,"title":"","content":"It doesn't have to be Erebus. You can use a cleansing ritual of your choice. But for the purposes of this exercise, say that the one in question is completely cleansed of Wyrm taint. Is it possible? What happens if you do?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T17:16:37-07:00","id":743278,"title":"","content":"In that case it begs the question of how taint works in your game?<br /> Do the things have an intrinsic level of taint for just being what they are?<br /> Are vampires creatures of the weaver or the wyurm in your game?<br /> <br /> Mechanics wise the lower a vampires humanity is the more tainted it is, so does the rite of cleansing restore the lost humanity levels or just cause it a crisis of conscience?<br /> <br /> Really it's your call because there are no rules for it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T17:26:54-07:00","id":743295,"title":"","content":"Clean it with fire, and all that's left is ash.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T17:27:33-07:00","id":743296,"title":"","content":"That depends on what you think vampires are in the cosmology of Werewolf.<br /> Sharing your head with a being of destruction and hunger that can take over your body and receiving supernatural boons sounds suspiciously like a Fomor to me - and what usually happens if you remove their corruption is that they die. Particularly if they should by rights be a corpse and are only animated by supernatural powers.<br /> However, there are sources that indicate that a high-humanity vampire doesn't register as Wyrm-tainted. I don't think this makes any sense considering that even if they love rainbows and kittens they're still animated bloodsucking corpses. You don't get much closer to the spiritual embodyment of death, consumption and corruption than that.<br /> But if you should decide that the Wyrm taint isn't an absolutely inherent and necessary part of vampirism, you'd likely get a vampire who finds it relatively easy to raise their humanity and who may have lost the Beast (as with Animalism \u00b0\u00b0\u00b0\u00b0\u00b0)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T17:33:44-07:00","id":743305,"title":"","content":"The description for the Rite of Cleansing in W20 states that it can't purify creatures of the Wyrm, whose taint is innate, instead causing them pain. It specifically mentions vampires as a creature to which that happens.<br /> You can think of the taint that can be Cleansed as a sort of spiritual sticky goop that clings to people and things who have been too near the Wyrm. Anything else is beyond the scope of a Level 1 rite.<br /> <br /> I've never had occasion to really htink about how I would handle the situation, since I don't like mixing games and I had vampiresonly appear briefly and rarely as one-time antagonists.But I think I'd go with a vampire being intimately Wyrm-tainted, in increasing amounts based on age and depravity. No need to muck with Humanity score and Golconda in my games which tend to be werewolf-centric; teh best vampire will always be a creature of the Wyrm and the best ways to purify it involve fire, the sun and separating his head from his everything else.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29-vidyaraja","name":"Vidyaraja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T18:42:30-07:00","id":743443,"title":"","content":"I will be gladly joining the PURGE IT WITH FIRE bandwagon. Vampires are a plague that needs to be exterminated, and practically everything they stand for and what they draw power from is antithetical to shapeshifters. They would have zero inclination to help them beyond relieving them of unlife.<br /> <br /> Now. There is one special case. Let's say that a character gets vamped that really shouldn't have been - a father, a brother, a wife. Let's say that that character shows an amazing level of restraint, and that the other Garou is so beset by grief (and so endowed by excessive willpower) to actually decide that he wants to cure them, no matter the fact that him attempting it will likely alienate him from his pack and the Garou Nation. <span style=\"font-size:8px\">That person is going to die horribly while protecting their loved one.</span><br /> <br /> But lets say they don't. Their commitment is absolute, they persuaded someone somehow to help them. Their solution has to be within the boundaries of Werewolf (no Mages, Mummies or Pikachus). The way I see it, such a Garou would have to cover the ends of the Earth seeking lost lore and learning of what exactly made the vampires and how their curse is transferred (n.b. this might not actually be the story from Vampire, but something more resonant with Werewolf). Upon learning more about the vampiric state and the underlying causes, a quest should be undertaken into the Umbra to find the entity that has cursed them and bargain with it to cure this one. Another option would be getting a Gurahl to help - if anyone can cure such a horrible thing, one of them can. But consider that it's going to make the Death Bear rite look trivial in comparison. Another option would be to go into Pangea and actually gain attention of Gaia - if they manage that, I'm sure the old girl wouldn't mind helping such a pair whose love is so true. Of course, actually getting her to react would require something monumental considering how much her own horrifying demise seems to phase her.<br /> <br /> All of these are about curing vampirism. I do not believe that you can purge a vampire of its fundamental taint due to the combination of three factors<ul><li>they are still undead and therefore unnatural and a pox upon existence</li> <li>worse yet they will always need blood to keep themselves going</li> <li>The Beast stays with you and it truly makes you want to do really, really bad things</li> </ul><br /> <br /> If you eliminate the taint, you will have to eliminate the undeath, the taking of life from others and the beast. The Creature you will have after that will no longer be a Vampire by any definition.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T18:53:12-07:00","id":743459,"title":"","content":"Purging a Vampire of Wyrm taint is essentially the same as restoring their Humanity and eliminating the Beast. This can't be done mechanically or by magic unicorns. Garou, at best, would bystanders during that vampire's own story to Golconda, Obeah, or whatever impossible quest is done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T18:59:02-07:00","id":743462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But consider that it's going to make the Death Bear rite look trivial in comparison. </div> </div> </div>Actually, the Death Bear rite might be exactly what is needed. Kill the vampire (preferably in a body-preserving way), challenge Mangi over the corpse and return the person to actual life, assuming the vampire state didn't do anything to the soul that can't be reversed - which seems likely, considering vampires produce completely normal (if slightly ashtray-prone) wraiths upon death.<br /> Of course, the end result is a normal living human (or kinfolk or Garou), not some kind of half-vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T19:27:00-07:00","id":743501,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I think I will also be climbing onto the Kill-the-Wyrm-tainted-blood-drinking-pseudo-fomor-with-fire,-sunlight,-claws-or-whatever-else-is-handy bandwagon as well. As noted above, purging a vampire of its &quot;taint&quot; (Wyrm-aspected or otherwise) also strikes me as being beyond the scope of a Lvl 1 Rite. (And let's not even get into the logistical and/or practical barriers to getting an undead creature into the Middle Umbra, as opposed to the more-possible-but-still-not-easy-for-vampires-to-access Lower Umbra/Underworld.)<br /> <br /> A vampire registers to Sense Wyrm if its Humanity score is 6 or lower. But the Beast is something that is innate to the vampire condition. Every vampire who has not achieved Golconda (assuming Golconda is not a myth) will feel the strain of the Beast inside their souls (assuming vampires even have souls). The Beast is essentially a supercharged id that rules over the baser instincts of a vampire. Must feed. Must sleep. Must fight or flee. That's it. And every vampire, whether on a Path of Enlightenment or on Humanity, is absolutely terrified of losing herself to the Beast. but since the Beast is such a fundamental part of vampire nature, it can't really be purged. Even vampires in Golconda don't get rid of their Beasts, they just managed to accept the Beast as a fundamental part of their natures, assuming they passed their suspires (no easy feat, and you only get one chance).<br /> <br /> No one can force a vampire to be more humane. No one can force a vampire to feel remorse for her crimes. No one can force a vampire to seek redemption. The vampire in question either honestly and truly seeks to redeem herself or she doesn't. It has to come from within, not without.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/835/7xu8.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/folderview?id=0By9UuUWWH6CiMVlhWHMwNWcyaG8&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Complete Garou Gifts List, Fera Gifts List, Garou Totems List and other assorted OPP/White Wolf goodies</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","name":"Su-tehp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2710_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T00:36:04-07:00","id":743941,"title":"","content":"I agree, the state of a vampire's (or person's in general) soul should not be modified by external use of a magic ritual on them. Freeing one from Wyrm corruption would most likely involve a death/rebirth process that results in them becoming something other than vampires, like what happened to the Children of Osiris.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T01:21:15-07:00","id":743964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/743149-purging-a-vampire-of-wyrm-taint?p=743941#post743941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree, the state of a vampire's (or person's in general) soul should not be modified by external use of a magic ritual on them. Freeing one from Wyrm corruption would most likely involve a death/rebirth process that results in them becoming something other than vampires, like what happened to the Children of Osiris.</div> </div> </div> </div>From a spiritual/werewolf point of view, what would such Wyrm-removal look like, exactly? Make the former bloodsuckers cease being mockeries and turn them into some weird flavor of Kami?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T04:09:43-07:00","id":744195,"title":"","content":"Vampires have souls in their own line. That's what you drink when you commit diablerie, after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T17:09:41-07:00","id":745349,"title":"","content":"That assumes Vampire stuff being true, it might as well be the primal power of ELDER BLOOOOOOD! Or maybe the mystical power of the Last Drop - the difference between life and (un)death! In general, Werewolf doesn't really deal with souls per se. (n.b. the WoD doesn't deal with souls in general. It's always being mentioned in kids glvoes and they were trying not to give any definitive answers, the DIablerie thing is probably one of the most definitive statements about souls in all of WOD bar Mummy)<br /> <br /> But it's less about them having or not having souls, and more about the fact that whatever they are, they are actually serving the Eater of Souls just by the fact they are existing. Their society and the way they treat people pretty much just feeds into the narratives that create banes and fomori. The ones that are off the deep end and on (most) paths of enlightenment are even worse in their effect on their surroundings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T17:13:07-07:00","id":745354,"title":"","content":"Well, vampires can also become wraiths, which also kind of needs a soul. Plus, vampires can sell their souls to infernal beings. There's plenty of support for vampire souls. Not that you're really arguing with me, I was just throwing information out there.<br /> <br /> I am not sure I would go so far as to say they serve the Eater of Souls just by existing. I would say that their existence <i>benefits</i> the Eater of Souls, but vampires aren't particularly servants to anything except perhaps the curse and each other. But I say this primarily because all the examples of Wyrm servants in Werewolf actively serve the Wyrm - like the Pentex BoD and Fomori and Black Spiral Dancers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T17:29:52-07:00","id":745393,"title":"","content":"Ah, but is a Wraith a soul or a memory? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> (And yeah, I'm arguing this bit in jest only because there isn't really a clear definition of a soul in the wod and what and how actually happens with it)<br /> <br /> Serving the Eater of Souls doesn't require you to have a membership card a uniform and to go around praising our Wyrmish lord. It only requires you to do certain things. Eater of Souls is about consumption, grinding, greed and placing your own self above all other things. It's about slowly chipping away all that is human and replacing it with something... else. Does that remind you of anyone?<br /> <br /> The nature of the Vampire is actually reinforcing the Eater just by them doing what they have to do to survive and hide among humanity. It's even worse if they are depraved maniacs in addition to that or if they casually wreck human lives for their own amusement. Those broken people are victims and their suffering breeds more banes and more fomori. It's a vicious cycle even without the vampires making it more messed up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T17:34:03-07:00","id":745415,"title":"","content":"Actually, directly serving any part of the Triatic Wyrm kind of <i>does</i> need a membership card and a uniform. There's a broad chasm between &quot;serving one part of the Triatic Wyrm&quot; and existing in a way that benefits it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T17:50:50-07:00","id":745443,"title":"","content":"Vampires aren't of the wyrm in the same way a Black spiral dancer, Bane or Formori is, but rather in the same way your average greedy bastard is. They are creatures of the material that spread violence, suffering, pain all sorts of wyrmy stuff. Its like the difference between a Tree and a Tree Spirit. The Wyrm is a very big and powerful spirit. Vampires are material things that it represents.<br /> <br /> Cleansing the wyrm from a vampire would cut off its connection to that spiritual quality, but because Vampires are far more complex than a tree there are other things for it to connect to. For a period of time the vampire would be much like as if it lost its beast or as if quelled, it would have all the advantages and disadvantages of such. Eventually though it would reconnect to the wyrm because well its there and the natural state of a Vampires are to connect to the wyrm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T17:57:47-07:00","id":745477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/743149-purging-a-vampire-of-wyrm-taint?p=745415#post745415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, directly serving any part of the Triatic Wyrm kind of <i>does</i> need a membership card and a uniform. There's a broad chasm between &quot;serving one part of the Triatic Wyrm&quot; and existing in a way that benefits it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah, that's what makes the war so messed up. You serve the Wyrm by doing petty, nasty shit. A guy who runs a sweatshop in Vietnam serves the Eater of Souls. The Garou who destroys the legacy of the other breeds serves the Defiler. The bitter teacher pouring his derision and abuse on kids serves the Eater of Souls. The private security corporation that helps &quot;fix&quot; problems all over the world serves the Beast of War.<br /> <br /> Your intent and alliegence are irrelevant. By doing bad unto others you create more bad. This &quot;bad&quot; breeds things that feed on the badness creating even more badness. That's the reason why humans are so scary and dangerous. That's the reason why the Garou are losing the war. And that's probably why the only way the Apocalypse could ever be prevented is if you managed to get humans to be better. To think of others and to work for making a better place.<br /> <br /> And that's why whenever the Garou act like stupid, aggressive, petty dicks... the Wyrm smiles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T18:03:11-07:00","id":745481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cogliostro</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/743149-purging-a-vampire-of-wyrm-taint?p=745477#post745477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nah, that's what makes the war so messed up. You serve the Wyrm by doing petty, nasty shit. A guy who runs a sweatshop in Vietnam serves the Eater of Souls. The Garou who destroys the legacy of the other breeds serves the Defiler. The bitter teacher pouring his derision and abuse on kids serves the Eater of Souls. The private security corporation that helps &quot;fix&quot; problems all over the world serves the Beast of War.<br /> <br /> Your intent and alliegence are irrelevant. By doing bad unto others you create more bad. This &quot;bad&quot; breeds things that feed on the badness creating even more badness. That's the reason why humans are so scary and dangerous. That's the reason why the Garou are losing the war. And that's probably why the only way the Apocalypse could ever be prevented is if you managed to get humans to be better. To think of others and to work for making a better place.<br /> <br /> And that's why whenever the Garou act like stupid, aggressive, petty dicks... the Wyrm smiles.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I disagree, there's a difference between Serving the wyrm and promoting the wyrm. A Black Spiral Dancer serves the wyrm. It is tainted. A Garou who frenzies and kills Kitsune for being uppity promotes the wyrm. They wyrm smiles at both, but the wyrm smiles MORE for the BSD and that's what wyrm taint is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T18:08:41-07:00","id":745488,"title":"","content":"Actually I'd posit that the Wyrm gets much more traction and power from the common people then it does from its dedicated agents. This is why the Wyrm cares much more about the human evil then about the strange shit that directly serves it. The BSD's and the Banes cannot help themselves, it's their nature to be horrible. They Wyrm couldn't care less about them, because with them the job is done. Humans and the Shifters... now they are the ones that have chosen to do what they do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T18:12:28-07:00","id":745491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cogliostro</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/743149-purging-a-vampire-of-wyrm-taint?p=745477#post745477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nah, that's what makes the war so messed up. You serve the Wyrm by doing petty, nasty shit. A guy who runs a sweatshop in Vietnam serves the Eater of Souls. The Garou who destroys the legacy of the other breeds serves the Defiler. The bitter teacher pouring his derision and abuse on kids serves the Eater of Souls. The private security corporation that helps &quot;fix&quot; problems all over the world serves the Beast of War.<br /> <br /> Your intent and alliegence are irrelevant. By doing bad unto others you create more bad. This &quot;bad&quot; breeds things that feed on the badness creating even more badness. That's the reason why humans are so scary and dangerous. That's the reason why the Garou are losing the war. And that's probably why the only way the Apocalypse could ever be prevented is if you managed to get humans to be better. To think of others and to work for making a better place.<br /> <br /> And that's why whenever the Garou act like stupid, aggressive, petty dicks... the Wyrm smiles.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I still don't really see that as &quot;serving the Wyrm&quot;. <br /> <br /> I guess we agree that this is a thing that benefits the Wyrm, but we don't agree on what to call it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T18:16:01-07:00","id":745494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/743149-purging-a-vampire-of-wyrm-taint#post743149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What have you done with the idea of purging vampires of their Wyrm taint? What <i>would </i>you do with it? Say you take a vampire to the endless silver night of Erebus and plunge them into the molten silver lake. She emerges whole, unbroken by trial, perhaps reforged instead. What happens? Does the vampire gain more control over her Beast? Does she become a creature wholly different from what she was before? Good or ill, what do you think happens with the vampire?</div> </div> </div> </div>Some time ago, I did something like this. The PC (bona-fide Camarilla vampires) had stumbled on a Fomori team and thinking they were some Tzimisce-creeps (the city was under a Sabbat assault, at the time...) destroyed them, recovering a strange &quot;relic&quot; (indeed, it was a powerful Fetish the fomori had freshly recovered).<br /> Problem was a couple of them were infected by some wyrmish-mold (the one from the Book of the Wyrm). A couple days later, they were on the run from the Sabbat with the two seriously ill (something appalling, for a leech).<br /> <br /> At a gas station, they stumbled on a werewolf pack. The Garou were stalking the station, trying to find heavy-tainted travellers and deal with them (furthermore, the spirits in the area where in turmoil, sensing the powerful Fetish).<br /> Fortunately, the alpha was a philodox they dealed with before (the type of deal &quot;don't kill each other, but kill the big bad monster- no, not the Nossie, the other one&quot;) and he identified the infection.<br /> While the 3 Garou could maybe kill all the five kindred and take the Fetish, the philodox did prefer not to kill &quot;things&quot; that battled the &lt;true Wyrm&gt; by his side (or so he said).<br /> As such, they struck a deal: the Garou would make a rite for cleansing the two Kindred from the taint, and the Kindred would surrender the Fetish.<br /> Main point is, the cleansing ritual was supposed to be made under sunlight. Stretching the ritual (the theurge was a Gnawers, so he knew how adapt things when in a pinch), they made it so the sunlight didn't need to actually touch the subject.<br /> While enjoying the ritual trying to resist the Rothshreck (vampire's Fox Frenzy) the two experienced an inner rebirth, then running like the hell because they needed to go somewhere safe before the sun would be totally up (they were in a thick grove).<br /> <br /> Aside from cleansing the mold, in the following days the two enjoyed a renewed closeness to their &quot;non-wyrmish&quot; side (the human one),<br /> I staged it so the characters would notice little things they would previously disregarded: the perfection of nature, innocent human acts, ignobile acts they could prevent and so on. The, giving free will to the players.<br /> This effect lasted less than a full moon, and while one of them ignored it, the other used these &quot;sparks&quot; for reattuning himself with his human side. It was a great playing, and the character is actually a funny one, as he is a Gargoyle with Humanity 8, which means he is a big rocky, horned, winged bloodsucker that do not register as &quot;of the Wyrm&quot; to shapeshifters.<br /> As a hobby he began painting and now his haven is plastered with paintings of tree, birds and cafes.<br /> He then learned Obfuscate (a Discipline that let the user disappear or alter his appearance), and in his free time is actually using it for helping humans... \u00b0__\u00b0<br /> One time he beaten to a pulp the thugs trying to bag-snatching a granny and then helped her crossing the road...<br /> -_-''","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>====================================<br /> &quot;Worst English-language User&quot; 2011-2015, 2017 running for the 2018<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ed6RV6Z.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div></div> </div> </div>","edited":{"userid":515,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/515-ryoga84","user":"Ryoga84","date":". 10-31-2015, 09:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/515-ryoga84","name":"Ryoga84","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T19:33:28-07:00","id":745590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cogliostro</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/743149-purging-a-vampire-of-wyrm-taint?p=745488#post745488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually I'd posit that the Wyrm gets much more traction and power from the common people then it does from its dedicated agents. This is why the Wyrm cares much more about the human evil then about the strange shit that directly serves it. The BSD's and the Banes cannot help themselves, it's their nature to be horrible. They Wyrm couldn't care less about them, because with them the job is done. Humans and the Shifters... now they are the ones that have chosen to do what they do.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I disagree. BSDs and Banes are direct servants. They are the Tools of the wyrm in a direct fashion. WIcked humans aren't direct tools, more a passive thing like farming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T19:51:23-07:00","id":745621,"title":"","content":"I think Cogliostro is right that passive observance does a lot more for the Wyrm than direct servitude, although some of the direct servitors help encourage and foment that passive observance (like say Pentex's various branches).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T20:04:55-07:00","id":745631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/743149-purging-a-vampire-of-wyrm-taint?p=745621#post745621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Cogliostro is right that passive observance does a lot more for the Wyrm than direct servitude, although some of the direct servitors help encourage and foment that passive observance (like say Pentex's various branches).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Passive stuff is what the wyrm gets for free. its Just free. Its nice to have but its not an active work?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T20:09:39-07:00","id":745642,"title":"","content":"Of course it's not active work but there is a <i>lot</i> of it, and it has inertia. <br /> <br /> Like, uhm, a corporation doesn't need to be actively serving the wyrm to dump pollutants into the local groundwater. Several corporations do this, and have caused severe health problems for people living in their vicinity. This does a lot for the Wyrm without being active servitude.<br /> <br /> And that's where I differ from Cogliostro in that I do not think that everyone who does anything that benefits the Wyrm is an active servant of the Wyrm. I mean if you're going to run a Werewolf game that way say goodbye to moral ambiguity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T21:00:14-07:00","id":745679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/743149-purging-a-vampire-of-wyrm-taint?p=745642#post745642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course it's not active work but there is a <i>lot</i> of it, and it has inertia.<br /> <br /> Like, uhm, a corporation doesn't need to be actively serving the wyrm to dump pollutants into the local groundwater. Several corporations do this, and have caused severe health problems for people living in their vicinity. This does a lot for the Wyrm without being active servitude.<br /> <br /> And that's where I differ from Cogliostro in that I do not think that everyone who does anything that benefits the Wyrm is an active servant of the Wyrm. I mean if you're going to run a Werewolf game that way say goodbye to moral ambiguity.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I kind of agree. I mean Garou need to deal with both, but Serving the wyrm's interests are the not the same as being a wyrm servant. So that's how i see Vampires and other entropic things.. they might spread the wyrm's interests but they aren't tools/servants.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T02:08:46-08:00","id":746220,"title":"","content":"This is bleeding from the other thread. I think the actual word we use the describe humanity's role is quite moot. And it's not about moral ambiguity, it's about moral responsibility. After all... The Only Thing Necessary for the Triumph of Evil is that Good Men Do Nothing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T02:49:41-08:00","id":746241,"title":"","content":"Moral ambiguity in this sense meaning that literally anyone could be more morally complex than pure evil... and the latter is where &quot;they all serve the wyrm&quot; seems to lead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T22:36:19-08:00","id":748504,"title":"","content":"I think I have a better way to explain this. Kindred are material. They are very material they are practically blind to the concept of all the other worlds out there. They can force their way in but its not a &quot;natural&quot; part of their setup.<br /> <br /> The Wyrm is a Spirit. A great and powerful spirit but a spirit none the less. Just as Grandfather Thunder is not responsible for every Storm that exists and all storms do not &quot;Serve&quot; him they generally a natural pheomenon that feeds somewhat into his portfolio. <br /> <br /> Kindred have that sort of relation with the wyrm. They are things in the physical world that feed the wyrm by existing, like acts abuse or a dirty car engine. They are just a &quot;Natural&quot; part of the world of Darkness that feeds the Spirit that is Corruption.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-02T08:31:52-08:00","id":749227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/743149-purging-a-vampire-of-wyrm-taint?p=746241#post746241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Moral ambiguity in this sense meaning that literally anyone could be more morally complex than pure evil... and the latter is where &quot;they all serve the wyrm&quot; seems to lead.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't have to be pure evil, but if they are of the Wyrm, then that thing is affiliated with the enemy. Garou are a warrior race, and in that sense they aren't like the other supernaturals. The Garou were created for war, and as such they should be able to identify their opponents in that war. The challenge (and ambiguity) comes from the fact that in the modern world, the Wyrm has its talons in all sorts of things- the werewolves can't raze whole cities, so they must pick and choose their battles. There is nothing wrong with them having the ability to sense tainted things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-02T10:23:04-08:00","id":749439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/743149-purging-a-vampire-of-wyrm-taint?p=746241#post746241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Moral ambiguity in this sense meaning that literally anyone could be more morally complex than pure evil... and the latter is where &quot;they all serve the wyrm&quot; seems to lead.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is kind of the point of moral ambiguity in Werewolf. The world is fucked up and it's guardians didn't do their job. They are forced into terorrism and asymetrical warfare because the whole world is wrong. Worse yet, the guardians themselves are flawed. The way to fix it is not by murdering everything that is tainted by the Wyrm (because everything is), it's to harness your nature and teach yourselves and others to be better and stand together against the horror that seeks to devour all that is and ever will be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-02T17:25:19-08:00","id":750310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/743149-purging-a-vampire-of-wyrm-taint?p=749227#post749227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It doesn't have to be pure evil, but if they are of the Wyrm, then that thing is affiliated with the enemy. Garou are a warrior race, and in that sense they aren't like the other supernaturals. The Garou were created for war, and as such they should be able to identify their opponents in that war. The challenge (and ambiguity) comes from the fact that in the modern world, the Wyrm has its talons in all sorts of things- the werewolves can't raze whole cities, so they must pick and choose their battles. There is nothing wrong with them having the ability to sense tainted things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sense wyrm senses wyrm taint, it doesn't specify &quot;of the wyrm&quot; or not, and there's a lot of stuff that could lead to tainting innocents. In a large number of possible cases, sensing wyrm is the starting point, not the end point. It's not the point of &quot;everything that smells of the wyrm must be killed&quot; but the point of &quot;why are these people tainted? What is the cause?&quot;<br /> <br /> If you're just slaughtering everyone that smells of the wyrm, you're playing Murderhobos: The Apocalypse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T00:46:31-08:00","id":750882,"title":"","content":"You don't kill vampires because they smell of the Wyrm, you kill them because they are vampires. Everything smells of the Wyrm, the whole thing about Sense Wyrm is that it's a setting statement and a critique of simplistic effects like Sense Evil.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T05:35:22-08:00","id":751197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cogliostro</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/743149-purging-a-vampire-of-wyrm-taint?p=750882#post750882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't kill vampires because they smell of the Wyrm, you kill them because they are vampires. Everything smells of the Wyrm, the whole thing about Sense Wyrm is that it's a setting statement and a critique of simplistic effects like Sense Evil.</div> </div> </div> </div>Incorrect, you kill them because they are undead, not vampires. They are &quot;of the Wyrm&quot; because they died and come back to life (or unlife).<br /> The Ananasi too are &quot;vampires&quot; (they feed on blood), but do not register automatically as &quot;of the Wyrm&quot;, they are simply distasteful and creepy.<br /> On the same note we can speculate that high Huymanity levels make the vampire akin to &quot;living&quot; again, and as such he &quot;appear&quot; less undead and as such do not register as &quot;of the Wyrm&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>====================================<br /> &quot;Worst English-language User&quot; 2011-2015, 2017 running for the 2018<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ed6RV6Z.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div></div> </div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/515-ryoga84","name":"Ryoga84","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T06:16:36-08:00","id":751241,"title":"","content":"High Humanity Vampires are still off the Wyrm. They just don't show up on Sense Wyrm. And Vampires are Vampires. Ananasi are bloodsucking spiders who are quite natural (for values of natural inherit in Werewolf).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T06:28:04-08:00","id":751263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cogliostro</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/743149-purging-a-vampire-of-wyrm-taint?p=751241#post751241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">High Humanity Vampires are still off the Wyrm. They just don't show up on Sense Wyrm. And Vampires are Vampires. Ananasi are bloodsucking spiders who are quite natural (for values of natural inherit in Werewolf).</div> </div> </div> </div>That is pretty much reiterating exactly what Ryoga was saying. in post #37. Did you mean to imply something else? <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T07:59:24-08:00","id":751455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Derzhuzad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/743149-purging-a-vampire-of-wyrm-taint?p=751263#post751263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is pretty much reiterating exactly what Ryoga was saying. in post #37. Did you mean to imply something else?</div> </div> </div> </div>It was mostly about preventing the usual furtherance of arguments about humanity and sense wyrm that follow by concluding that 7+ Vampires are sunshine and rainbows and only want to save the world from evil by helping mages and their furry friends(which is already in the topic running side by side to this one). Also, labeling Ananasi as vampires is quite... missing the point.<br /> <br /> I may be overly pedantic over this as the topics over the last few days have taken a turn for utterly cringeworthy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T18:18:58-08:00","id":752659,"title":"","content":"Err... ok, my bad, English is not my primary language, so I often misspeak<br /> <br /> For &quot;vampire&quot; I mean &quot;bloodsucker&quot;, kindred are vampires, ananasi are bloodsucker and therefore vampires and blood-eating bats are called vampires.<br /> As such we can guess that blood-eating is not of-the-wyrm, it could be distasteful, but not impure enough to be considered of-the-wyrm, and it's in the natural order of the things. That said, if the concept of &quot;bloodsucker&quot; is not of-the-wyrm, the problem is somewhere else.<br /> and is in the fact that the kindred are undead, and that is the discriminant, they rise from the grave (or from the sewers or from wherever) and sunlight and fire are banes for them, but this is related to the fact they are undead, not bloodsuckers. Evidence for this fact is that Western Garou treat each undead as of-the-wyrm , be they Kindred, Kuei-Jin or Risen.<br /> <br /> Going to the opposite extreme, we can even speculate that a race of living vampires would not be sensed inerently of-the-wyrm (even though individual members could well be).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>====================================<br /> &quot;Worst English-language User&quot; 2011-2015, 2017 running for the 2018<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ed6RV6Z.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div></div> </div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/515-ryoga84","name":"Ryoga84","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T18:48:21-08:00","id":752739,"title":"","content":"Rising from the dead and feeding on the blood of the living is pretty unnatural.<br /> <br /> Ananasi's feeding is based on their arachnid biology, so it gets to be natural, yeah. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T18:55:09-08:00","id":752743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/743149-purging-a-vampire-of-wyrm-taint?p=752739#post752739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rising from the dead and feeding on the blood of the living is pretty unnatural.<br /> <br /> Ananasi's feeding is based on their arachnid biology, so it gets to be natural, yeah. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>A rather messed up reading of arachnid biology meant to introduce gimmicky traits resembling those from another game, really, but the result is the same end point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T19:03:52-08:00","id":752790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/743149-purging-a-vampire-of-wyrm-taint?p=752743#post752743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A rather messed up reading of arachnid biology meant to introduce gimmicky traits resembling those from another game, really, but the result is the same end point.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That is true and I can't argue with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T05:24:02-08:00","id":753756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/743149-purging-a-vampire-of-wyrm-taint?p=752739#post752739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rising from the dead and feeding on the blood of the living is pretty unnatural.<br /> <br /> Ananasi's feeding is based on their arachnid biology, so it gets to be natural, yeah. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Bats too, but isn't a little problematic defining what is &quot;natural&quot;? After all, Fomori too are &quot;natural&quot; as created by the Wyrm, which is a member of the Triat, same for the Gorgons (and this mean half cheetah and half gazelle super-beasts)<br /> <br /> I'm not saying kindred aren't of-the-wyrm. They are and will always be (even though high levels of Humanity can lessen their wyrmish attitudes), what I'm saying is that the biologic act isn't unnatural per se, it's only aggravating, but not the main point of the vampire existence (from Gaia point of view), if exist somewhere else you can't discount it as &quot;unnatural&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>====================================<br /> &quot;Worst English-language User&quot; 2011-2015, 2017 running for the 2018<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"